# CQ-28 · geometry-endpoints
#
# Question: For each spatial fact, do the figure and the ground carry the
#           bounding boxes a geometry check would need to decide it?
# Persona:  P1 — generation-pipeline engineer. Before the fourth gate can say
#           anything, both endpoints have to carry a rectangle; this is the
#           coverage question that says how often it can.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.10 (`vso:bbox2d`); §5.13 (geometry consistency);
#           §5.13.6 (the `no-geometry` verdict)
# Form:     SELECT — one row per spatial fact
# Note:     Every box column comes back UNBOUND, and that is the finding:
#           §5.13.7 records it in prose — "no gallery scene carries both a
#           rectangle and a spatial fact" — and this is the same measurement,
#           re-derivable by anyone with a SPARQL engine. The one scene with
#           rectangles asserts no relation over them, so the geometry gate
#           decides nothing on this corpus and its positive fixture is what
#           keeps `make geometry-check` from being vacuous.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?fact ?figure ?figureBox ?ground ?groundBox
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?fact a vso:SpatialFact ; vso:figure ?figure ; vso:ground ?ground .
    OPTIONAL { ?figure vso:bbox2d ?figureBox }
    OPTIONAL { ?ground vso:bbox2d ?groundBox }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?fact
